// REQUIRES: host-linux-amd64 || host-linux-arm64
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/run-golden.py --src %S/Inputs/own/lent.gopp %S/Inputs/own/lent.out
// GOLDEN: by-hand
// P04.09 review R1: a value lent to an interface parameter (TYP-7: the
// tagged itab and a copy in the caller's frame) is boxed on every way it can
// leave the parameter and outlive the call: a closure that captures the
// parameter, `move(v)` into an append, into a literal, out of a return, and
// a swap into a package variable (`gopp.iface_take`). Each value is read
// after its caller returned and the stack was written over. Under
// `check-run-leaks` a tagged value that escaped is a stack use after return.
